Why Is Demand Increasing
Rising Tooth Loss Burden — Tooth loss remains the fundamental demand driver for implant-based fixed restoration, creating a large addressable patient population across aging and adult populations.
Digital Dentistry Adoption — Intraoral scanning, CBCT planning, guided surgery, CAD/CAM prosthetics, and connected digital workflows are improving treatment planning and workflow integration.
Expanding Treatment Access — Greater dental-service availability, local implant manufacturing, financing options, and growing clinical capacity are expanding access to implant treatment across emerging markets.

Clinical & Technology Watch: Digital Implant Workflows Gain Importance
Dental implant treatment is increasingly connected to digital diagnostics and restorative workflows. Clinics can integrate imaging, intraoral scanning, computer-guided placement, implant planning, CAD/CAM design, and chairside manufacturing into a more coordinated treatment pathway. This is shifting competition beyond the implant fixture itself toward integrated systems and digital ecosystems.

